  "modelAnswer": "1 point: evidence is mostly general, and commentary summarises the evidence without explaining how it supports the argument. 2 points: some specific, relevant evidence, and commentary that explains how some evidence relates to the argument, but no line of reasoning is established or it is faulty. 3 points: specific evidence to support all claims in a line of reasoning, and commentary that explains how some of the evidence supports a line of reasoning. 4 points: the same evidence requirement, with commentary that consistently explains how the evidence supports a line of reasoning. Between 3 and 4 the evidence requirement does not change at all — only the consistency of the commentary does, which is a coverage measure rather than a quality measure. The cap: writing that suffers from grammatical and/or mechanical errors that interfere with communication cannot earn the fourth point in this row.",
