  "prompt": "A synthesis response opens with a sentence that only rephrases the prompt's own framing. Its body quotes four of the six sources, each quotation specific and each followed by commentary that ties it to the writer's position, and the essay repeatedly explores a genuine tension between two of the sources as part of its argument. Score it row by row and justify each row.",
