  "effect": "Matching grammar tells the reader that the matched items are of equal weight, before the reader has thought about whether they are. A list that is not parallel forces the reader to work out how the items relate; a parallel list hands the relationship over free. That is why parallel prose feels controlled and why claims made inside it feel already settled — the reader has been given a shape to agree with rather than an argument to test.",
  "confusedWith": "anaphora",
