  "effect": "Three is the smallest number that reads as a pattern rather than a pair: the first item sets a shape, the second confirms it, the third either completes it or breaks it. Because a group of three feels finished, a tricolon makes a partial case sound exhaustive — the reader stops expecting a fourth item and therefore stops asking what a fourth item might have been. That is a persuasive effect, not an ornament, and it is what commentary should say.",
