  "exampleAttr": "Original — written for this study site.",
  "effect": "Once a process has intentions, it can be blamed. That is the whole move: a budget cannot choose a victim, but a sentence that says it did converts an outcome nobody signed into an act somebody committed. Personification is therefore rarely decorative in argument — it is usually an assignment of responsibility made without the writer having to name a person or prove intent.",
