  "id": "asyndeton",
  "term": "Asyndeton",
  "family": "syntax",
  "def": "A list or sequence with the conjunctions deliberately left out, items separated only by commas.",
  "example": "We cut the routes, the shelters, the wardens, the maps.",
  "exampleAttr": "Original — written for this study site.",
  "effect": "Removing the conjunctions removes the ranking a conjunction imposes: no item is marked as last, so the list reads as an extract from something longer that the writer simply stopped reciting. It also speeds the line, because there is nothing to pause on. The combined effect is accumulation without closure — the reader finishes the sentence with the sense that more could have been said.",
  "confusedWith": "polysyndeton",
