  "exampleAttr": "Original — written for this study site.",
  "effect": "Each \"and\" is a small stop, so the sentence slows and every item gets weighed on its own instead of dissolving into a list. Depending on what is being listed, the result is either relentlessness or exhaustion — the reader is made to feel the length of the sequence rather than just be told it. That felt duration is the effect; \"it emphasises the list\" is not.",
  "confusedWith": "asyndeton",
